Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/gregbook/readpng.c
Line: 273
Function: readpng_get_image
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: The allocation size uses rowbytes*height where both are png_uint_32. The multiplication is performed in 32-bit arithmetic and can overflow before being passed to malloc (size_t). The preceding guard compares against SIZE_MAX and will not detect this 32-bit overflow on 64-bit platforms. This can under-allocate image_data, after which png_read_image will write height rows of rowbytes each via row_pointers, causing a heap buffer overflow. For example, a large but valid image (e.g., width≈65535, RGBA => rowbytes≈262140; height≈100000) yields a true size≈26 GB that overflows 32-bit to ~444 MB, leading to out-of-bounds writes.

Source context:
